* text=auto eol=lf

*.blade.php diff=html
*.css diff=css
*.html diff=html
*.md diff=markdown
*.php diff=php

/.github export-ignore
CHANGELOG.md export-ignore
.styleci.yml export-ignore

# deploy/ is checked out on Linux and must keep LF endings regardless of the
# platform it was edited on. This is not cosmetic: a shell script with CRLF
# fails on Linux with "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M", and systemd and cron are
# similarly unforgiving about a trailing carriage return.
#
# These rules used to live in a .gitattributes at the root of the combined
# repository, above the Laravel app, because Laravel's own file could not reach
# up to deploy/. Since the split the two are in the same repository, so they are
# one file -- which is better, because the rule and the thing it protects are
# now impossible to separate by accident.
deploy/*            text eol=lf
deploy/deploy.sh    text eol=lf
deploy/*.cron       text eol=lf
deploy/*.service    text eol=lf
deploy/*.example    text eol=lf
